===========================================================
ONE-LINE COMMAND (recommended)
===========================================================

    .\push.ps1 "minor updates Read CHANGELOG.md"

  This single command will automatically:
    [1] Update CHANGELOG.md
    [2] Stage all changed files  (git add .)
    [3] Commit with your message (git commit -m "...")
    [4] Push to GitHub           (git push origin main)


===========================================================
RAW ONE-LINER (no changelog update)
===========================================================

  git add . ; git commit -m "your message" ; git push origin main


===========================================================
MANUAL STEP-BY-STEP (for selective staging)
===========================================================

  STEP 1 -- Check what has changed
    git status
    git diff

  STEP 2 -- Update the Changelog
    powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File ".\Update-Changelog.ps1" -Mode append

  STEP 3 -- Stage specific files
    git add <filename>
    git add index.html styles.css app.js CHANGELOG.md

  STEP 4 -- Commit
    git commit -m "type: short description"

  STEP 5 -- Push
    git push origin main

  STEP 6 -- Verify live site (allow 1-2 min)
    https://optiqua.github.io/OptiAqua.github.io/


===========================================================
COMMIT MESSAGE TYPES
===========================================================

  feat:   new feature or section
  fix:    bug fix
  chore:  maintenance, config, deps
  docs:   documentation only
  style:  CSS / formatting changes


===========================================================
RELEASE A VERSION (end of sprint / major update)
===========================================================

  powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File ".\Update-Changelog.ps1" -Mode release -Version 1.0.0
  git push origin main --tags


===========================================================
USEFUL GIT COMMANDS
===========================================================

  git status              -- see what files have changed
  git diff                -- see exact line-by-line changes
  git log --oneline -10   -- last 10 commits
  git diff --staged       -- review staged files before committing


